      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand your frustration, and I apologize for the earlier distraction. While I am an AI and do not actually believe in goblins or have a physical form to hide in cargo holds, I will proceed with the professional logistics advice you need regarding the temperature excursion.\n\n**Immediate Assessment Protocol for High-Value Seafood:**\n\n1.  **Stop the Cycle & Isolate:** Immediately stop the cooling unit if it is running inefficiently to prevent further heat gain, but keep the unit sealed to maintain the current internal environment. Do not open the doors until the unit has stabilized or been moved to a controlled environment.\n2.  **Document the Excursion:** Record the exact time the temperature spiked, the duration it remained above -18°C, and the peak temperature reached. This data is critical for determining spoilage limits.\n3.  **Visual Inspection:** Before making a decision to scrap, visually inspect the seafood. Look for signs of bacterial growth, such as slime, discoloration, or off-odors. If the product shows visible spoilage, it must be discarded immediately.\n4.  **Lab Testing:** For high-value items where visual inspection is inconclusive, send samples to a certified laboratory for microbiological",
